        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_987196875.1",
        "comments": "The assembly bCirCya1.hap1.1 is based on 62x Oxford Nanopore data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project (https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial Oxford Nanopore assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. MicroFinder was used to order scaffolds prior to curation. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. This genome has been assembled using ONT and HiC data and phased. The result is two curated haplotypes. Chromosomes Z and W were identified by copy number in the diploid assembly. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 2 (hap1 1.0 Mbp - 17.4 Mbp, hap1 1.9 Mbp - 18.7 Mbp) are unknown.",
